M. The mass of moving air. A piston of the skin's size in a wall carries air 8a/(3 pi) deep: 66 g/m^2, or 0.265 of the bare skin's weight per area.
   Laid evenly on the lowest mode alone (first order, the mode's shape with its air unchanged), it lowers that mode by:
   the 1954 disc (B = 0.839): 2.0% (the bare skin's share of the mode's moving mass is 0.148)
   the reference drum's 40-ring load of 4 skins, tuned (B = 0.330): 0.7% (the bare skin's share of the mode's moving mass is 0.049)
   the reference drum's 40-ring load of 4 skins, free (B = 0.359): 0.9% (the bare skin's share of the mode's moving mass is 0.070)
   the reference drum's 40-ring load of 4 skins, tabla (B = 0.352): 0.9% (the bare skin's share of the mode's moving mass is 0.068)
   The (1,1) mode carries air too, less of it, and that would lower the note as well; I have not computed it. So the lowest mode's place is lowered by less than these figures.
